
### 1. Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/health


### 2. Get all leads
GET http://localhost:3000/leads


### 3. Get one lead
GET http://localhost:3000/leads/1


### 4. Filter leads by status
GET http://localhost:3000/leads?status=contacted


### 5. Create a lead successfully
POST http://localhost:3000/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Lead",
  "email": "testlead@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company"
}


### 6. Create a lead with an invalid email
POST http://localhost:3000/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid Lead",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "company": "Test Company"
}


### 7. Create a lead with an unknown field
POST http://localhost:3000/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unknown Field Lead",
  "email": "unknown@example.com",
  "company": "Test Company",
  "unexpectedField": "not allowed"
}


### 8. Update a lead's status successfully
PATCH http://localhost:3000/leads/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "qualified"
}


### 9. Update a lead with an invalid status
PATCH http://localhost:3000/leads/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending"
}


### 10. Use an invalid lead ID
GET http://localhost:3000/leads/abc


### 11. Get a lead that doesn't exist
GET http://localhost:3000/leads/999999


### 12. Delete a lead
DELETE http://localhost:3000/leads/1


### 13. Send malformed JSON
POST http://localhost:3000/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":


### 14. Request an unknown route
GET http://localhost:3000/unknown-route
